-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 1ב, §1.36 הבחירות לכנסת
-- Temporary provisions for the elections to the tenth Knesset: political
-- activity, fundraising, criticism of the Knesset and the government,
-- election propaganda, and standing as a candidate.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `1.36 הבחירות לכנסת`

@desc The actor of section 1.36 that the shared Party list lacks.
DECLARE `1.36 party` IS ONE OF
    `the Government`

@desc A teaching employee, as far as section 1.36 asks about it.
DECLARE `employee in the election` HAS
    `is a state employee`                         IS A BOOLEAN
    `in supervision or instruction on a Civil Service Commission post` IS A BOOLEAN @desc employed in supervision or instruction on a post of the Civil Service Commission's establishment
    `holds administrative authority`              IS A BOOLEAN @desc see `administrative authority` below (section 1.36.2(d), second paragraph)
    `has a post involving contact with the public` IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `forum` IS ONE OF
    `a press conference`
    `an interview with a journalist`
    `a speech in a public place`
    `a broadcast`
    `a newspaper`
    `a book`
    `another forum`

DECLARE `body criticised` IS ONE OF
    `the Knesset or its committees`   @desc including the laws and decisions they adopted
    `the Government or its ministries` @desc including its policy

DECLARE `election action` IS ONE OF
    `organise a political demonstration or procession`
    `solicit, collect or receive donations` HAS
        `for the state treasury by virtue of office` IS A BOOLEAN
        `permitted by the Government`                IS A BOOLEAN
    `criticise` HAS
        `whom`               IS A `body criticised`
        `in a way that insults or injures` IS A BOOLEAN
        `where`              IS A `forum`
    `permit a barred fundraising for a public purpose` HAS
        `generally rather than for a particular case` IS A BOOLEAN
    `take part in Knesset election propaganda`
    `host or speak at a house circle for Knesset election propaganda`

-- F-1.36-a: the heading makes the section temporary provisions for the
-- elections to the tenth Knesset (30 June 1981), yet the takanon still
-- publishes them. This file reads them as the takanon's standing rules for
-- Knesset elections; read as headed, they bind no later election.
GIVEN `Knesset number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provisions apply to the elections to Knesset` `Knesset number` IF
    `Knesset number` AT LEAST 10

GIVEN `Knesset number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the provisions apply if read as headed, as temporary` `Knesset number` IF
    `Knesset number` EQUALS 10

`the heading and the standing reading differ for a later Knesset` MEANS
    NOT (`the provisions apply to the elections to Knesset` 25
         EQUALS `the provisions apply if read as headed, as temporary` 25)
#ASSERT `the heading and the standing reading differ for a later Knesset`

§§ `1.36.1 הקדמה`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_1__subpara_a
`the day of the tenth Knesset elections` MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY 30 6 1981

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_1__subpara_b
GIVEN e IS AN `employee in the election`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `addressed by section 1.36` e IF
    e's `is a state employee`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_1__subpara_c
GIVEN e IS AN `employee in the election`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Civil Service Regulations apply instead` e IF
    e's `in supervision or instruction on a Civil Service Commission post`

§§ `1.36.2 פעילות מדינית ומפלגתית ופעילות הקשורה בבחירות`

-- (א) and its second paragraph: every teaching employee, of every grade,
-- seniority and post. F-1.36-b: whether "every teaching employee" reaches
-- beyond the state employees section 1.36.1(b) addresses.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_a akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_a/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `election action`
DECIDE `no political demonstrations` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `organise a political demonstration or procession`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.36.2(a): a teaching employee does not organise a demonstration or procession of a political character"

GIVEN e IS AN `employee in the election`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bound by the demonstrations rule` e IF
    `addressed by section 1.36` e

GIVEN e IS AN `employee in the election`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bound by the demonstrations rule if "every teaching employee" is literal` e IF
    TRUE

`a teacher employed by a local authority` MEANS
    `employee in the election` WITH
        `is a state employee`                                             IS FALSE
        `in supervision or instruction on a Civil Service Commission post` IS FALSE
        `holds administrative authority`                                  IS FALSE
        `has a post involving contact with the public`                    IS TRUE

`the two scopes of the demonstrations rule differ for a non-state teacher` MEANS
    NOT (`bound by the demonstrations rule` `a teacher employed by a local authority`
         EQUALS `bound by the demonstrations rule if "every teaching employee" is literal` `a teacher employed by a local authority`)
#ASSERT `the two scopes of the demonstrations rule differ for a non-state teacher`

-- F-1.36-c: clauses (2) and (3) of (ב) refer to "ס\"ק (א)"; the
-- prohibition they qualify is (ב)(1), and (א) of section 1.36.2 is the
-- demonstrations rule. Read as (ב)(1).
-- The exception "permitted" is the Government's permission of (ב)(3),
-- encoded below.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_b__cls_1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_b__cls_4
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `election action`
DECIDE `no fundraising` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `solicit, collect or receive donations` `for the treasury` `permitted`
          PROVIDED (NOT `for the treasury`) AND (NOT `permitted`)
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.36.2(b)(1): a teaching employee does not raise, collect or receive donations, except for the state treasury by virtue of office or as the Government permits for a public purpose"

-- (ב)(3): the Government may permit the barred action for a public
-- purpose, generally or for a particular case.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_b__cls_3
GIVETH A DEONTIC `1.36 party` `election action`
DECIDE `the Government's permission` IS
    PARTY `the Government`
    MAY   `permit a barred fundraising for a public purpose` `generally`

-- The other reading of "(א)": the Government's power to permit reaches the
-- demonstrations of (א), and the fundraising ban has no exception.
GIVEN `read (א) as section 1.36.2(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government may permit a demonstration` `read (א) as section 1.36.2(a)` IF
    `read (א) as section 1.36.2(a)`

`the two readings of "(א)" differ on permitting a demonstration` MEANS
    NOT (`the Government may permit a demonstration` FALSE EQUALS `the Government may permit a demonstration` TRUE)
#ASSERT `the two readings of "(א)" differ on permitting a demonstration`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_b__cls_2
GIVEN `permitted under section 25 of the Wage Protection Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the deduction from salary is one section 25 of the Wage Protection Law, 1958 permits
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deduction is not barred by the fundraising rule` `permitted under section 25 of the Wage Protection Law` IF
    `permitted under section 25 of the Wage Protection Law`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_c__cls_1 akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_c__cls_2
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `election action`
DECIDE `no insulting criticism` IS
    PARTY `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `criticise` `body` `insulting` `place`
          PROVIDED `insulting` AND NOT (`place` EQUALS `another forum`)
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.36.2(c): a teaching employee of any grade does not criticise the Knesset or the Government in an insulting or injurious way in public"

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_d
GIVEN e IS AN `employee in the election`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `election action`
DECIDE `no election propaganda` e IS
    IF `in the class barred from propaganda` e
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         SHANT `take part in Knesset election propaganda`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.36.2(d): a teaching employee with administrative authority or contact with the public takes no part in Knesset election propaganda, in public or not, anywhere"
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN e IS AN `employee in the election`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `in the class barred from propaganda` e IF
    e's `holds administrative authority` OR e's `has a post involving contact with the public`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_d/p2
GIVEN `power to decide matters for members of the public` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the power, by law or not, carries the force to decide matters concerning members of the public
      `supervises holders of statutory powers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `power to take steps not anchored in law` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `administrative authority` `power to decide matters for members of the public` `supervises holders of statutory powers` `power to take steps not anchored in law` IF
    `power to decide matters for members of the public` OR `supervises holders of statutory powers` OR `power to take steps not anchored in law`

@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_e/p1
GIVEN e IS AN `employee in the election`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `election action`
DECIDE `no house circles` e IS
    IF `in the class barred from propaganda` e
    THEN PARTY `the teaching employee`
         SHANT `host or speak at a house circle for Knesset election propaganda`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "section 1.36.2(e): a teaching employee with administrative authority or contact with the public does not host or speak at a house circle for Knesset election propaganda"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_e/p2 The heading of the next topic ("3 הצגת מועמדות לכנסת"), printed as a paragraph of (ה).

-- Section 56(b) of the Knesset Elections Law, as the takanon reports it.
@ref akn:chp_1ב__sec_1_36__hc_2__para_2__subpara_e/p3
`a Knesset candidate must stop service when the list is submitted` MEANS FALSE

-- Worked examples.
#ASSERT `in the class barred from propaganda` `a teacher employed by a local authority`
#ASSERT NOT `a Knesset candidate must stop service when the list is submitted`
#ASSERT `administrative authority` FALSE FALSE TRUE

#TRACE `no fundraising` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `solicit, collect or receive donations` FALSE FALSE AT 2
#TRACE `no insulting criticism` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the teaching employee` DOES `criticise` `the Government or its ministries` FALSE `a newspaper` AT 2
